E196                             ; "/" ( a b -- q r ): the remainder is on top. Truncates toward zero; r takes
E196                             ; a's sign. Divide |a| by |b|, then q gets the sign of a XOR b and r the sign
E196                             ; of a. Unchecked, dividing by zero returns two cells of no meaning; checked,
E196                             ; it stops with Z.
E196                             ; b's cell is dropped once D holds |b|; udiv then leaves the remainder just
E196                             ; where that cell was, so stepping X back down makes it the top cell.
E196                          IF   CHECKED   
                    E_ZERO:   LDA   #"Z"   ; divide by zero, the stack as it was
                              JMP   error   
