E1EB                             ; Backspace takes the last character back (and is echoed as it is), CR ends
E1EB                             ; (stored, not echoed), every other key is stored and echoed until the line
E1EB                             ; is full. Y = the length so far; T0 = the most allowed.
E1EB   20 13 E1     LINE:     JSR   neg   ; TOS = the count, and A = its high byte
E1EE   D0 04                  BNE   ln0   
E1F0   B5 00                  LDA   0,X   
